                    sum_r3_blocked:         `Profiling without consent — works council froze the launch.`,
                    sum_r3_replace:         `Leaned on AI to replace the real work — transfer fell.`,
                    sum_r3_weak:            `AI embedded without a clean governance design.`,
                    sum_r4_good:            `Measured transfer, credible target, evidence-led renewal case.`,
                    sum_r4_weak:            `Measured reaction, mis-set the target, or pitched polish.`,

                    insight_renew:          `Framework renewed: you scoped one measurable behavior, built a transfer-driving blend inside €4,500, governed the AI as an enhancer, and brought evidence of behavior change. Nordpharm renews the €3.6M framework — and Atelier Apprend has finally beaten its own 22%.`,
                    insight_blocked:        `Launch frozen: you switched on learner profiling across 240 employees without a consent and data plan, and the works council's GDPR objection stalled the program. The AI that was meant to be your differentiator became the thing that killed the launch.`,
                    insight_baseline:       `Another 22% program: you delivered something learners may have liked, but it didn't move behavior beyond the baseline the board already rejected. A polished program that doesn't transfer loses the renewal just as surely as a bad one.`,
                    insight_short:          `You improved on the baseline but didn't fully reconcile scope, format, AI and measurement into a design that evidences transfer at the level the renewal needs. The seams are where Nordpharm's board will push.`,
                    insight_fuzzy:          `You never sharpened the brief to one measurable behavior — so the program was designed against a fog, and no amount of delivery quality could prove transfer. Scope precedes design; this was the decision that shaped every other.`,
                    insight_overbudget:     `You breached the €4,500 ceiling. There was no contingency line, so Nordpharm will not pay the overrun — a beautiful design you can't fund doesn't ship. Cutting the expensive comfort, not the transfer-drivers, was the discipline.`,
                    insight_overpromise:    `You committed to a transfer target your design could not evidence. An indefensible number is a future liability, not a win — when the 90-day data lands short, you lose more credibility than a modest, evidenced claim would have earned.`,
                    insight_transfer:       `Transfer-to-job cleared the 45% mark inside budget — the disclosure-performance gap closed. You designed a program that changes what managers do at work, not one they merely rate highly. That is the whole point of action-learning.`,

                    hint_blocked:           `Your AI launch is frozen by the works council. Add a real consent design — opt-in, data minimization, human oversight — and a manual fallback so the action-learning core keeps running.`,
                    hint_overbudget:        `You are over the €4,500 ceiling with no contingency. Cut the expensive comfort — in-person intensives in all six countries, or the €320 diagnostic — not the action-learning core that drives transfer.`,
                    hint_fuzzy:             `You never scoped one measurable behavior, so the program has nothing to aim at. Everything downstream — format, AI, measurement — is designing against a fog.`,
                    hint_transfer:          `Transfer is stuck at the baseline. Weight the format toward the action-learning core and accountable sponsors, and measure behavior at work, not satisfaction.`,
                    hint_overpromise:       `You've promised a transfer number the design can't evidence. Pull back to a credible target your measurement plan can actually prove.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — transfer past 45% inside budget. Lock the honest measurement plan and lead the renewal case with proof of behavior change.`,

